# Puzzle_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Puzzle-driven games (puzzle_adventure).

## 2. This document owns
- Puzzle taxonomy (logic/spatial/observation/combination) and authoring patterns.
- Difficulty curve targets and hint ladder design (what unlocks which hint).
- Solvability guarantees (no dead states, reset semantics).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Interaction mechanics used by puzzles — Interaction_Design.
- Room/space layout — Level_Design.
- Narrative framing — Script / Bible.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Puzzle philosophy / 2. Taxonomy / 3. Authoring patterns / 4. Difficulty curve / 5. Hint ladder / 6. Reset & fail states / 7. Accessibility fallbacks / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Puzzle vs Interaction: puzzle = authored challenge; interaction = reusable mechanic.
- Puzzle vs Level: rules here, physical placement there.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every puzzle lists its required verbs; all exist in the interaction table.
- Every puzzle has a fail/reset path and a hint ceiling.
